-- title:
--   Inertial charpolys at a ramified principal-series prime, v_q(M)=2
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$, let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform in the project's sense (a normalised eigenform whose good eigensystem occurs at no proper divisor of $M$), let $\lambda$ be a prime, $S$ a finite set of naturals containing $\lambda$ and every prime divisor of $M$, and let $\mathcal O'$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation ring, adically complete for its maximal ideal, with finite residue field and with $\lambda$ in its maximal ideal. Let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism from the weight-two Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(M)$ generated by the chosen Hecke generators away from $S$) to $\mathbb C$ with $\chi_g(T_\ell)$ the $\ell$-th $q$-expansion coefficient of $g$ for every prime $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$, and let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the range of $\chi_g$ to $\mathcal O'$. Let $q\ne\lambda$ be a prime, let $\Phi\ne 0$ be a function on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the adeles of $\mathbb Q$ which is an adelic lift of $g$ (invariant under global points on the left, invariant under the finite level-one subgroup at level $(M)$ on the right, and equal to the weight-two slash of $g$ evaluated at $i$ on elements trivial at the finite places with positive-determinant archimedean part), let $\mu_1,\mu_2:\mathbb Q_q^\times\to\mathbb C^\times$ be characters, and let $f\ne0$ be a nonzero $\mathbb C$-linear, $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_q)$-equivariant map from the adelic span of $\Phi$ to the principal-series carrier $B(\mu_1,\mu_2)$. Assume $\mu_1^{-1}\mu_2$ is ramified, i.e. not identically $1$ on the norm-one units of $\mathbb Q_q$, and that the exponent of $q$ in $M$ equals $2$. Then there is a characteristic-zero adically complete discrete valuation ring $\mathcal O''$ with finite residue field, an $\mathcal O'$-algebra which is module-finite over $\mathcal O'$ with $\mathcal O'\to\mathcal O''$ local and injective, and a two-dimensional adically continuous $\mathcal O''$-representation $\rho$ of $\operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ such that: for every prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group of $A$ acting as $x\mapsto x^\ell$ on the residue field, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))X+\ell$ (the Hecke value taken in $\mathcal O''$); and there is a function $a$ from the Galois group to $\mathcal O''^\times$ such that for every valuation subring $P$ with $q$ a nonunit and every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup of $P$ over $\mathbb Q$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ equals $(X-a(\sigma))(X-a(\sigma)^{-1})$ and, for all $n$, $a(\sigma)^n=1$ if and only if $\mu_1$ of the image in $\mathbb Q_q^\times$ of the $q$-adic cyclotomic character of $\sigma$ raised to the $n$-th power equals $1$.
--
--   This is the local–global compatibility statement on inertia at $q$ (Carayol's theorem in the principal-series case) in the form used here: it produces one $\lambda$-adic realisation of the Hecke eigensystem of $g$ whose inertial characteristic polynomials at $q$ are $(X-a(\sigma))(X-a(\sigma)^{-1})$ with $a(\sigma)$ of the same multiplicative order as $\mu_1$ evaluated on the cyclotomic character, specialised to level exponent $v_q(M)=2$. It feeds the statement [`CuspForm.IsNewform.exists_charpoly_inertia_eq_and_pow_eq_one_iff_of_linearMap_psCarrier_ne_zero_of_factorization_eq_two`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsNewform.exists_charpoly_inertia_eq_and_pow_eq_one_iff_of_linearMap_psCarrier_ne_zero_of_factorization_eq_two), on the way to the level-lowering input at the prime $q$.
